&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who We Are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;VML is a global creative company that combines brand experience, customer experience, and commerce to create connected brands&amp;nbsp;that drive growth. Guided by a&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Human First&lt;/strong&gt; philosophy, VML is known for its innovative work for brands and consistently ranks among the world’s leading creative companies, including the WARC Creative 100.&amp;nbsp;VML’s global network spans 55+ markets with principal offices in Buenos Aires, Kansas City, London, New York, São Paulo, Shanghai and Singapore.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;VML is part of WPP, the trusted growth partner for the world&#39;s leading brands. Powered by exceptional talent and our agentic marketing platform WPP Open, WPP unites cutting-edge media intelligence and data solutions, creativity, production, enterprise solutions and expert strategic counsel.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For more information, please visit&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.vml.com/&quot; data-outlook-id=&quot;d4b7d1c3-8ad6-4b6d-ab45-d3cb5a3aebe1&quot;&gt;www.vml.com &lt;/a&gt;and follow along on  &lt;a href=&quot;https://urldefense.proofpoint.com/v2/url?u=https-3A__urldefense.com_v3_-5F-5Fhttps-3A_www.linkedin.com_company_vml_-5F-5F-3B-21-21JboVxjCXSME-21OhlpCfbkl1UcWPwns1-2DGtvHOzFh0QwHV49fsPgGw-2DVCCU1bCg8aQFI9vN-2Dy-2DVwaQcITH2j2XKzGKBIFRLYf2AUWVYY1dFGK6-24&amp;amp;d=DwMFaQ&amp;amp;c=euGZstcaTDllvimEN8b7jXrwqOf-v5A_CdpgnVfiiMM&amp;amp;r=zouFnm4jZMgDFaYF1uVcRY3rbgHWPca_luUrBUkT6Yc&amp;amp;m=QzcCgXCAOjzj5hiU48_CKOdHRSJ4_YpuqfviT9yjlzH5VrkzySTZ-WaQXlYAnj4W&amp;amp;s=jJ7q5V70u9oUx7ONPm5jC3IK8y6vxDilX6BGTlqlWlA&amp;amp;e=&quot; data-outlook-id=&quot;a3ef68bf-16fb-4ebc-9ca9-406007d6cefc&quot;&gt;LinkedIn&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;#WeAreVML.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h1&gt;Director, Analytics &amp;amp; Marketing Intelligence – Automotive&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Company:&lt;/strong&gt; VML / WPP&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt; London, UK&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Working Model:&lt;/strong&gt; Hybrid working&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reporting to:&lt;/strong&gt; Chief Marketing Intelligence Officer&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About the Opportunity&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;We’re looking for a &lt;strong&gt;Director, Analytics &amp;amp; Marketing Intelligence&lt;/strong&gt; to lead analytics and marketing intelligence across a major European automotive business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;This is a senior, client-facing leadership role for someone who combines &lt;strong&gt;deep automotive experience with strong expertise in marketing analytics, data and consulting&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;You’ll be responsible for helping clients make better, more informed marketing and business decisions through data and insight. You’ll work closely with senior stakeholders across markets, bringing together local and regional perspectives, identifying opportunities for growth and shaping solutions that deliver genuine commercial value.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;The role requires someone who can operate comfortably at both a strategic and commercial level — someone who can understand complex business challenges, translate data into a clear point of view, and turn that thinking into compelling propositions, new opportunities and long-term client partnerships.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Marketing Intelligence &amp;amp; Analytics Leadership&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;false&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the development and delivery of marketing analytics and intelligence across European markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turn complex data, customer behaviour and market information into clear, actionable insights and recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advise senior client stakeholders on how data and analytics can support marketing effectiveness, customer growth and broader business objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring together different sources of data and intelligence to create a consistent, holistic view of performance across markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify emerging trends, opportunities and challenges within the automotive sector and translate these into meaningful recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help shape new approaches, products and capabilities across analytics, measurement and marketing intelligence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Client Leadership &amp;amp; Consulting&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;false&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build trusted relationships with senior client stakeholders, acting as a strategic advisor rather than simply a delivery partner.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand individual market challenges while maintaining a strong regional perspective.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead senior-level conversations around business performance, marketing effectiveness, customer behaviour and growth opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate complex analytical thinking in a clear, compelling and commercially relevant way.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Challenge existing thinking where appropriate and bring new perspectives, ideas and approaches to the client.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Commercial Growth &amp;amp; Business Development&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;false&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify opportunities to grow existing relationships and develop new areas of work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shape propositions, scopes of work and commercial opportunities around client needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead or support pitches, proposals and new business conversations across the European automotive landscape.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own commercial considerations including scoping, financial management and account profitability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with wider WPP and agency teams to bring the right capabilities together around client opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build a strong understanding of client priorities and translate these into sustainable commercial growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Regional &amp;amp; Cross-Functional Leadership&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;false&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with local market teams to create a joined-up European approach to analytics and marketing intelligence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Connect specialists across data, strategy, media, technology, customer experience and creative to deliver integrated solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish consistent standards, ways of working and best practice across markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Share market intelligence and learnings across the wider organisation to strengthen capabilities and drive innovation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide leadership, direction and expertise to teams working across multiple markets and disciplines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What We’re Looking For&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;false&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Deep experience within the automotive sector&lt;/strong&gt; with a strong understanding of the industry, its customers, commercial challenges and marketing landscape.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extensive experience in &lt;strong&gt;marketing analytics, data, measurement and/or marketing intelligence&lt;/strong&gt;, ideally within an agency, consultancy or client-side environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience advising senior stakeholders and translating complex data into clear strategic recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong commercial understanding, with experience developing new opportunities, scopes of work and client relationships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of growing and strengthening senior client partnerships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working across multiple markets, ideally within a European or global organisation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong consulting and problem-solving skills, with the ability to move from a business challenge to a clear analytical and strategic response.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication and presentation skills, with the confidence to influence senior stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading cross-functional teams and bringing together different capabilities to solve complex client challenges.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong understanding of how data and analytics can influence marketing, customer experience and business performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable operating in a fast-paced, complex environment where priorities and client needs can evolve quickly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Additional European language skills would be an advantage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What&#39;s in it for you?&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;Aside from a generous annual leave allowance and pension allowances, you will have access to a whole host of other benefits and activities such as:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;false&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Life Assurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Permanent Health Insurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;BUPA&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible hybrid-working schedule&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enhanced family friendly policies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Well-being Programme&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Employee Assistance Support&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cycle to Work Scheme&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Eye Care and Glasses Vouchers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Season Ticket Loans&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;WPP Discounts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;You will also have a clear long-term career development plan and access to our learning and development activities and online learning platforms.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Our Commitment to Diversity, Equity &amp;amp; Inclusion&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;VML is an equal opportunity employer and considers applicants for all positions without regard to race, colour, religion or belief, sex, age, national origin, citizenship status, marital status, military/veteran status, genetic information, sexual orientation, gender identity, physical or mental disability.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;We believe in creating a dynamic work environment that values diversity and inclusion and strives to recruit a diverse slate of candidates to help us achieve that goal.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you are unable or limited in your ability to access our career site as a result of a disability, we will be happy to assist you. Please contact our People Team at &lt;a ---------- to request an alternate accommodation. Please note that only requests for an employment application accommodation will be returned.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;normaltextrun&quot;&gt;&lt;span lang=&quot;EN-GB&quot;&gt;&lt;span lang=&quot;EN-GB&quot;&gt;We believe the best work happens when we&#39;re together, fostering creativity, collaboration, and connection. That&#39;s why we’ve adopted a hybrid approach, with teams in the office an average of four days a week. If you require accommodations or flexibility, please discuss this with the hiring team during the interview process.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;normaltextrun&quot;&gt;&lt;span lang=&quot;EN-GB&quot;&gt;WPP (VML) is an equal opportunity employer and considers applicants for all positions without discrimination or regard to characteristics. We are committed to fostering a culture of respect in which everyone feels they belong and has the same opportunities to progress in their careers.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;scxw176048299&quot;&gt;&lt;span lang=&quot;EN-GB&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;When you click &quot;Submit Application&quot;, this will send any information you add below to VML. Before you do this, we think it&#39;s a good idea to read through our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.vml.com/recruitment-privacy-policy&quot;&gt;Recruitment Privacy Policy&lt;/a&gt;. California residents should read our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.vml.com/california-recruitment-privacy-notice&quot;&gt;California Recruitment Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;. This explains what we do with your personal data when you apply for a role with us, and, how you can update the information you have provided us with or how to remove it.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Summary:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Quotient is seeking an entrepreneurial, highly strategic Senior Director of Business Development to lead the company&#39;s partnering, asset in-licensing, and market intelligence activities. Reporting to the CFO, this individual will play a critical role in shaping the company&#39;s portfolio and business strategy, identifying external opportunities, and executing partnerships that create significant value for the company and its stakeholders.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal candidate combines strong scientific and commercial judgment with demonstrated transaction leadership and the ability to operate effectively in an early-stage, fast-paced, resource-constrained environment. This person will be equally comfortable evaluating an external asset, developing a market landscape, engaging with potential partners, and working cross-functionally with R&amp;amp;D, clinical, regulatory, and executive leadership.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for someone with a proven track record in Business Development within the biotech or pharmaceutical sectors with significant experience leading collaboration and in-licensing deals and demonstrated strategic thinking and relationship building experience.&amp;nbsp; On a personal level, Quotients enjoy a fast-paced environment, think like entrepreneurs, are adaptable, accountable, work proactively and look out for each other.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and execute a comprehensive business development strategy aligned with the company&#39;s scientific, clinical, and corporate objectives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify, evaluate, and cultivate relationships with potential pharmaceutical, biotechnology, academic, and other strategic partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead commercial partnership opportunities from initial identification and diligence through valuation, negotiation, deal structuring, and execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop compelling partnership materials, including opportunity assessments, strategic rationales, valuation analyses, and executive presentations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain a strong network across the biotechnology and pharmaceutical industries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify opportunities for co-development, licensing, collaborations, research partnerships, and other strategic transactions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support corporate strategy and financing activities by providing external market and competitive intelligence&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead identification and evaluation of external assets and technologies that could complement or expand the company&#39;s internal pipeline&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish systematic processes for sourcing and prioritizing in-licensing opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate cross-functional diligence with scientific, clinical, regulatory, IP, legal, and finance teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop business cases and recommendations for investment in external programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead negotiations around licensing economics, development responsibilities, milestones, royalties, territories, governance, and other key deal terms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain a forward-looking view of emerging technologies, mechanisms, therapeutic approaches, and platform opportunities relevant to the company&#39;s strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;u&gt;Essential&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced degree in life sciences, medicine, business, or a related field; MBA or equivalent business training is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of relevant experience in biotechnology or pharmaceutical business development, corporate strategy, licensing, or a related function&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience executing or materially contributing to biopharma partnership and licensing transactions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of drug development and the biotechnology/pharmaceutical industry&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience evaluating external therapeutic assets and conducting cross-functional diligence&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to perform or oversee market, competitive, and commercial analyses for drug development programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong financial and analytical capabilities, including familiarity with asset valuation, deal economics, forecasting, and scenario analysis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent negotiation, communication, and presentation skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong scientific and strategic judgment, with the ability to rapidly assess complex information and make clear recommendations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to build trusted relationships with senior executives and external partners across the biopharma ecosystem&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Entrepreneurial mindset and willingness to work hands-on in an early-stage environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Values and Behaviors:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Encourage respectful disagreement and cultivate open-minded, ego-free interactions to continuously push each other towards excellence&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Seek out diverse perspectives; practice active listening and genuine curiosity to ensure all contributions are valued, regardless of source&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recognize the impact of your behavior, language and attitudes, and strive for balanced, meaningful exchanges that enhance mutual growth and understanding in all interactions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use a company-first mindset to guide decision-making; prioritize team over individual success&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take calculated risks and challenge convention in the quest for exceptional outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Quotient:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Quotient Therapeutics is a privately-held, early stage company developing breakthrough medicines informed by natural somatic genetic diversity present in patients. Through our work in somatic genomics, we are forging a new status quo for biopharma research and development across a broad pipeline of internal and partnered programs.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The company was founded by Flagship Pioneering, an innovative enterprise that conceives, creates, resources, and grows first-in-category life sciences companies. Flagship Pioneering has created over 100 groundbreaking companies over the past twenty years, all of which are pioneering novel and proprietary biological, industrial, and engineering approaches to solve major needs in human health and sustainability. These companies include Moderna (MRNA), Generate Biomedicines, Sana Biotechnology (SANA), Tessera Therapeutics, Evelo Biosciences (EVLO), Indigo Agriculture, Seres Therapeutics (MCRB), and Syros Pharmaceuticals (SYRS).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Quotient Therapeutics and Flagship Pioneering are committed to equal employment opportunity regardless of race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital status, disability, gender identity or Veteran status.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Recruitment &amp;amp; Staffing Agencies:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Quotient Therapeutics (“Quotient”) and Flagship Pioneering (“FSP”) do not accept unsolicited resumes from any source other than candidates. The submission of unsolicited resumes by recruitment or staffing agencies to Quotient, FSP or their employees is strictly prohibited unless contacted directly by Flagship Pioneering’s internal Talent Acquisition team. Any resume submitted by an agency in the absence of a signed agreement will automatically become the property of FSP, and FSP will not owe any referral or other fees with respect thereto.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Privacy Notice for Applicants:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;When you apply for a role at Flagship Pioneering or one of its portfolio companies, we collect and use personal information you provide (such as your name, contact details, work history, and application materials) to evaluate your application, communicate with you, and comply with legal obligations. Your application data is processed through Greenhouse, our applicant tracking system, and may also be reviewed using AI-assisted screening tools. We do not sell your personal information. California residents have rights under the CCPA/CPRA including to know, delete, and opt out of the sharing of their personal information. If you are located in the EU or UK, we process your data under GDPR and you have rights to access, rectify, and erase your data. To exercise your rights or for questions, contact -----<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Ping Identity:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Ping Identity, we believe in making digital experiences both secure and seamless for all users, without compromise. We call this digital freedom. And it&#39;s not just something we provide our customers. It&#39;s something that inspires our company. People don&#39;t come here to join a culture that&#39;s built on digital freedom. They come to cultivate it.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our intelligent, cloud identity platform lets people shop, work, bank, and interact wherever and however they want. Without friction. Without fear.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;While protecting digital identities is at the core of our technology, protecting individual identities is at the core of our culture.&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.pingidentity.com/en/company/championing-every-identity.html&quot;&gt;We champion every identity.&lt;/a&gt; One of our core values, Respect Individuality, reminds us to celebrate differences so you are empowered to bring your authentic self to work.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re headquartered in Denver, Colorado and we have offices and employees around the globe. We serve the largest, most demanding enterprises worldwide, including more than half of the Fortune 100. At Ping Identity, we&#39;re changing the way people and businesses think about cybersecurity, digital experiences, and identity and access management.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Ping Identity is looking for a proactive Senior Field Marketing Manager to join the UKI region. This team has gone through a restructure in 2025 and while has the largest customer base in EMEA ,the objective is to drive geo growth in 2H 2026 and beyond.&amp;nbsp; There is considerable effort needed to boost brand awareness and create net new logo demand to achieve the regions’ ambitious growth targets.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This individual will be responsible for the UKI region, alongside a UKI Field Marketing Specialist. This innovative and forward-thinking marketing professional will partner closely with the UKI Sales leaders and Sales organisation and work with pan-EMEA Go To Market (GTM) teams to develop and implement a strategic integrated GTM plan, focusing on multi-touch campaigns that drive qualified pipeline.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Duty and Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Jointly work as part of the UKI leadership team and the Senior Manager Field Marketing for Northern Europe to develop the strategic approach required for success in region to drive exceptional growth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with internal parties and third-party vendors to develop and achieve our Go To Market vision in region&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Execute the UKI plan with clear focus on delivering the metrics of success&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage the day to day activity of the Field Marketing Specialist, ensuring growth and development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review, refine and develop the GTM tactics on a regular basis to ensure continued engagement and penetration into the named strategic accounts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with the Pan-EMEA Programmes lead to create and execute vertical or use case led GTM plans for Account Executives to an enterprise audience (ABM 1:Few, 1:1, Deal acceleration programmes,)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide articulate feedback on the campaigns, analysis of success and next steps&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate to the quarterly QBRs reporting on successes and outlining future strategies and tactics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Responsible for budget and procurement processes, auditing and accountability for budget spend and management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Desired Skills &amp;amp; Experience&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in marketing, business, or in a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A minimum of 2-3 years’ experience in Senior Field Marketing role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous experience in the IT industry, ideally in a technology B2B SAAS environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of current digital marketing technologies and techniques.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of SFDC and Marketo.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Great relationship building and negotiation skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills in English.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Positive attitude and work collaboratively.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical and problem-solving skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong initiative and ability to work independently and collaboratively.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Qualifications:&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A marketing or related business degree or equivalent&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Working Conditions:&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Travel – approximately 30% travel, mostly within the UKI region but some within Europe or US&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Remote working contract with occasional travel to our London and Bristol based offices to work alongside the regional Sales Development Reps&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Life at Ping:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe in and facilitate a flexible, collaborative work environment. We’re growing quickly, but remain true to the innovative, can-do startup values that got us here. Most importantly, we keep hiring talented, smart, fun, and genuinely nice people because that’s who we want to succeed with every day.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Here are just a few of the things that make Ping special:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A company culture that empowers you to do your best work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Employee Resource Groups that create a sense of belonging for everyone.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Regular company and team bonding events.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive benefits and perks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Global volunteering and community initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
